  "investigation_notes": "**Outcome: insufficient_evidence**\n\nUpload failure confirmed as persistent app unhealthy, but root-cause cannot be isolated with available evidence.\n\n**Evidence collected:**\n\n- App `incidentlab-app-1` is `running`, `Up 5 seconds` at initial check (E1), `running:true, exit_code:0, oom_killed:false` (E5)\n- DB `incidentlab-db-1` is `running`, `Up 10 seconds (healthy)` (E1), `health:healthy, running:true, exit_code:0, oom_killed:false` (E6)\n- App `/health` is `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` on first check (E2) and still `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` on repeat check (E12) - persistent, not single transient\n- App mount present: `type:bind source:/srv/lab-data destination:/data rw:true` (E5), `user:1000:1000` (E5)\n- DB and app share `networks: incidentlab_default` (E5, E6)\n- DB health transitions to `health_status: healthy` with `pg_isready` `exit_code:0` (E8)\n- Recent Docker events show orderly `destroy/rename/start` recreate at `2026-10-28T23:41:18Z` for db and `2026-10-28T23:41:24Z` for app, with `die exit_code:0` due to `kill/stop`, no crash exit (E8)\n- `restart_count:0` for both containers (E5, E6)\n\n**Ruled out with evidence:**\n\n- Host capacity on upload filesystem: `use_percent:9.0, inode_use_percent:0.2, available_mb:410.7` on `/srv/lab-data` (E3) - not full\n- Root filesystem full: `use_percent:6.8, inode_use_percent:1.5` on `/` (E11) - not full\n- Dependency container down: db is running and healthy (E1, E6, E8)\n- OOMKill / crash exit: `oom_killed:false, exit_code:0` (E5, E6)\n\n**Cannot rule in/out - data source unavailable:**\n\n- App logs unavailable (E7), DB logs unavailable (E9) - cannot see application error, DB connection error, or storage write error\n- Upload directory ownership/mode/writability for `1000:1000` unavailable for `/srv/lab-data/uploads` (E4) and for `/srv/lab-data` (E10) - permission/ownership cause for uploads cannot be assessed despite confirmed bind mount (E5)\n\nNo assumption made about log contents or directory permissions not seen.\n\nTo separate root-cause from symptom: app `503` (E2, E12) is a symptom; dependency db reports `healthy` (E6, E8) but app-to-db connectivity cannot be verified without logs (E7, E9 missing).\n\n**Next approved manual checks needed:** app logs, `ls -ldn /srv/lab-data/uploads`, write test as UID 1000, DB connectivity from app network.\n",
